{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JV2FynZCLC8UzU35uGUPE3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Shared `pkg/` libraries (sys, format, testutils) support `cmd/` utility packages. Each utility has a PRD, use case, test suite, and differential tests.\n\n**Current state:** Specifications through rel05.4 are complete. Code exists at generation tags for earlier releases. Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) has spec_complete status with no code started.\n\n**Current release:** rel05.4 — all four use cases (md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) need implementation.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 05.4 is the earliest incomplete release in scope. The four checksum utilities are structurally identical — each reads files/stdin, computes a hash using Go's `crypto/*` packages, and prints output in the standard `hash  filename` format with optional `--check` mode. They share no pkg/ dependencies beyond testutils and sys (SIGPIPE). All four fit within a single 150-250 line implementation task since each utility is ~40-50 lines of production code.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, cmd/sha512sum -- checksum quartet production code\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (PRDs for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for differential testing and SIGPIPE handling)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum utility using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum utility using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum utility using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum utility using crypto/sha512\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Each utility reads input from files listed on the command line or from\n          stdin when no files are given (or when \"-\" is specified). Compute the\n          hash using the corresponding crypto/* package and write output in GNU\n          coreutils format: lowercase hex hash, two spaces, filename (or \"-\" for\n          stdin). One line per input file. Follow PRD requirements for input handling.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement --check (-c) mode: read lines in \"hash  filename\" format from\n          a file (or stdin), recompute the hash for each listed file, and print\n          \"filename: OK\" or \"filename: FAILED\". Exit 1 if any check fails. Print\n          a summary warning to stderr if any lines failed. Follow PRD requirements\n          for --check behavior including --quiet, --status, and --warn flags if\n          specified by the PRD.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement --binary (-b) and --text (-t) flags. On this platform both\n          modes produce the same output since there is no text/binary distinction\n          on Unix. The --binary flag sets the mode indicator to \"*\" before the\n          filename; --text sets it to \" \". Default is text mode. Follow the PRD\n          for exact flag semantics.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() in each\n          utility per the shared SIGPIPE protocol. Handle --help and --version\n          flags: --help prints usage to stdout and exits 0; --version prints\n          version info to stdout and exits 0. Exit code is 0 on success, 1 on\n          any failure (missing file, failed check, malformed check line).\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          All four utilities share the same structure. Each main.go implements\n          the full utility independently -- do not create a shared internal\n          package. The code duplication is acceptable given each file is ~40-50\n          lines and a shared abstraction adds complexity without benefit for\n          four trivially similar programs.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Use Go standard library only: crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256,\n          crypto/sha512, encoding/hex, flag, fmt, io, os, bufio. Import\n          github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling.\n          Do not import pkg/format or any external dependency.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Follow the GNU coreutils output format exactly. Hash output is lowercase\n          hexadecimal. The separator between hash and filename is two spaces for\n          text mode, one space and asterisk for binary mode. When reading from\n          stdin, use \"-\" as the filename in output.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/md5sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/md5sum/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: cmd/sha1sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha1sum/\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: cmd/sha256sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha256sum/\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: cmd/sha512sum/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/sha512sum/\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          Each utility produces correct hash output for a known test input.\n          For example, \"echo -n hello | go run ./cmd/md5sum/\" outputs\n          \"5d41402abc4b2a76b9719d911017c592  -\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: |\n          Each utility supports --check mode: given a valid checksum file,\n          it verifies each entry and exits 0 when all pass, 1 when any fail.\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/md5sum/ ./cmd/sha1sum/ ./cmd/sha256sum/ ./cmd/sha512sum/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27607,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27607},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d50dbf9-ecc8-4948-9326-1d646d4520dd","uuid":"3f6d7200-d877-491d-a12b-42ac784e244e"}
